  "functions": [
    "FUNC.CUBEMEMBER"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "CUBEMEMBER holds the member's MDX identity in cell metadata, accepts array/range tuples returning the last caption, and coerces caption numbers and logicals to text",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, CUBEMEMBER(connection, member_expression, [caption]) displays the member's caption (or caption coerced to text: 123 -> \"123\", TRUE -> \"TRUE\", \"\" -> empty text), stores the MDX member identity in workbook mdxMetadata, accepts a range or array of expressions as a tuple (displaying the last member's caption, and returning #N/A if two members belong to the same hierarchy), and returns #N/A for an unknown connection, unknown member, number, or empty text. All 4,188 full-bank CUBEMEMBER rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in DnaCalc crates/calc-host/tests/fixtures/cube/measured.xlsx and pivot_cube/oracle.xlsx (Excel 16.0.20527); 4,188/4,188 full-bank rows match.",
